# An HTML page's `border-radius` on an `<img>` crops its picture (#1926):
# the import writes Word's Crop to Shape geometry (`a:prstGeom` ellipse
# or roundRect) and the view clips the picture to its corners. `doc`'s
# `flow.pictures.N` reads each body picture as the last frame built it:
# its `width`, `height` and clip `radius` (px), its `shape` and `round`
# (the radius is half the shorter side). The fixture's pictures are
# `data:` PNGs, so nothing resolves from disk: a round 32 px avatar in a
# rounded card cell (whose own `border-radius` is dropped, never text), a
# 120 x 40 picture with 8 px corners and a plain one. The read follows a
# `shot`, which waits for the frame.

test issue 1926 a rounded image is drawn clipped to its corners
  open copy:../fixtures/rounded-images.html
  assert view.layout is web
  call window-size {"w":1100,"h":800}
  shot window
  call doc {}
  assert reply.flow.pictures.0.shape is ellipse
  assert reply.flow.pictures.0.round is true
  assert reply.flow.pictures.0.width is 32
  assert reply.flow.pictures.0.radius is 16
  assert reply.flow.pictures.1.shape is roundRect
  assert reply.flow.pictures.1.round is false
  assert reply.flow.pictures.1.radius is 8
  assert reply.flow.pictures.2.shape is rect
  assert reply.flow.pictures.2.radius is 0
